#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124269 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/id #uuid "e9539818-ad55-5bb3-8c5d-5b85303f9e6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5521" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSuppose $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. The matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B} \\mid \\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\rightarrow W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in V$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are shown above. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}$." :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n[T(x)]_{C} &= [T]_{B \\mid C} \\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124270 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/id #uuid "8a371b65-8c57-5d10-88aa-2d4928fb028c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5522" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ (shown above) and a basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3$.\nThe matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B} \\mid \\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^3$ relative to these bases, and the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2$, are also given. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}$." :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n[T(x)]_{C} &= [T]_{B \\mid C} \\cdot [x]_{B}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$, the coordinates of $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$. So, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{x_{1} - 2x_{2} = 5; 4x_{1} - 5x_{2} = 2\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-4)R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -18\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}R_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n[T(x)]_{C} &= [T]_{B \\mid C} \\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124333 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "01b46867-ba6d-5085-9543-b77ded581194" :question/math-academy-id "e-8604" :question/problem "Suppose $\\mathbf{T}: V \\rightarrow W$ is a linear map and $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\}$ and $\\mathcal{C} = \\{\\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2 \\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B} \\mid \\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to these bases, if\n\n> $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1)=-3\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2,\\quad$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)=\\mathbf{c}_2-2\\mathbf{c}_1\\quad$ and $\\quad\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)=\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2$." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}T(b_{1}) =-3c_{1} + 5c_{2} & ⟹[T(b_{1})]_{C} = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(b_{2}) = c_{2} - 2c_{1} & ⟹[T(b_{2})]_{C} = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(b_{3}) = c_{1} + 5c_{2} & ⟹[T(b_{3})]_{C} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B} \\mid \\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1)$, $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124334 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "3d6b0aec-c282-581e-ae4a-560654d80e3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-8605" :question/problem "Consider the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3\\}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFind the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B} \\mid \\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$ relative to these bases if\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B} \\mid \\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1)$, $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)$, and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$.\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_i)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ for each $i=1,2,3$. We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\n\\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid; c_{1}\\begin{vmatrix}c_{2} & T(b_{1}) & T(b_{2})\\end{vmatrix}T(b_{3}); \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{1}:=(-1)R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{1}:=R_{1} + 4R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 11 & -29 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -29 & 25 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fcbabfa-1fe9-5f08-8951-f9a2d5561f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123281} {:answer/id #uuid "e29cafcc-9d49-52de-824c-7dbd724840eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123282} {:answer/id #uuid "0434b6ac-42db-58e8-b0a3-5665a50739df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\\\ -7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123283} {:answer/id #uuid "152e779f-53e2-50fd-bab4-22e91117cb3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123284} {:answer/id #uuid "59671841-cdb7-5c98-ab46-f543a1894970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "152e779f-53e2-50fd-bab4-22e91117cb3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123284} :answer-field/id #uuid "598a627c-d15d-5921-9ed0-40e687af2ded" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123280}] :question/id #uuid "a7a7dfc1-b352-5fd9-84db-53ec5b318168" :question/math-academy-id "q-38529" :question/problem "Suppose $T: V → W$ is a linear map and $B = {b_{1}, b_{2}}$ and $C = {c_{1}, c_{2}, c_{3}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B \\mid C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if\n\n$T(b_{1}) =-2c_{1} + 4c_{2} - 2c_{3}$ and $T(b_{2}) = 3c_{2} - 7c_{3} + c_{1}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "818adacf-5de1-5ff3-baad-2b566bc7745a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123287} {:answer/id #uuid "9f09a315-e267-5509-92e6-d7ea1c61480c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123288} {:answer/id #uuid "ba44948c-25a1-595f-b1fd-2ed3c12aa1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123289} {:answer/id #uuid "422f05be-d14b-5ca5-9eb4-1a47330fdb75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123290} {:answer/id #uuid "61960e4a-bae9-5df0-b19b-42ad67e92881" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "422f05be-d14b-5ca5-9eb4-1a47330fdb75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B \\mid C} = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123290} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef9e1063-283a-5bf6-9335-2aa39e25ec03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123286}] :question/id #uuid "1f9af258-e8a2-56a9-9f94-0fa33495c61f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38530" :question/problem "Suppose $T: V → W$ is a linear map and $B = {b_{1}, b_{2}, b_{3}}$ and $C = {c_{1}, c_{2}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B \\mid C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if\n\n$[T(b_{1})]_{C} = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}, [T(b_{2})]_{C} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}, [T(b_{3})]_{C} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/ti